WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.547 --> 00:00:03.515
how president Biden has been a

00:00:03.782 --> 00:00:04.783
friend for 40 years.

00:00:06.285 --> 00:00:07.319
I obviously, you've not always

00:00:07.586 --> 00:00:08.453
seen eye to eye on a lot of

00:00:08.787 --> 00:00:08.854
issues.

00:00:09.121 --> 00:00:10.789
He says that he wants signed a

00:00:10.856 --> 00:00:11.423
photo for you.

00:00:12.391 --> 00:00:13.559
I don't agree with a darn thing

00:00:13.826 --> 00:00:14.793
you say, but I love you.

00:00:15.327 --> 00:00:16.295
How do you describe your

00:00:16.795 --> 00:00:18.363
relationship when it comes to

00:00:18.797 --> 00:00:19.565
nobody is there, just you two

00:00:19.832 --> 00:00:20.332
on the phone?

00:00:20.799 --> 00:00:22.401
He's telling you what you need

00:00:23.302 --> 00:00:24.403
from each other.

00:00:24.803 --> 00:00:27.506
&gt;&gt; That's exactly what happens.

00:00:28.307 --> 00:00:29.608
We have been around the block

00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:32.144
so many times, we were the new

00:00:32.411 --> 00:00:33.412
kids on the block when he came

00:00:33.679 --> 00:00:35.280
in as a young senator from

00:00:35.547 --> 00:00:36.515
Delaware, and I came in as the

00:00:36.815 --> 00:00:38.450
young Israeli diplomat in the

00:00:38.817 --> 00:00:38.851
embassy.

00:00:39.384 --> 00:00:40.452
This was in 1982.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.821
We have known each other for a

00:00:42.821 --> 00:00:43.488
long time, 40 years.

00:00:44.289 --> 00:00:46.825
We speak openly to one another.

00:00:46.859 --> 00:00:49.394
I think the president Biden's

00:00:49.661 --> 00:00:50.362
commitment to Israel's real,

00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:56.435
it's not just words, it comes

00:00:56.835 --> 00:00:56.969
from the heart.

00:00:57.236 --> 00:00:59.338
My commitment aligns with the

00:00:59.605 --> 00:00:59.972
United States Israel.

00:01:00.305 --> 00:01:02.407
It has gone through many

00:01:02.841 --> 00:01:04.343
presidents, and it has to be

00:01:04.843 --> 00:01:05.377
bipartisan.

00:01:05.377 --> 00:01:05.644
I believe that.

00:01:07.279 --> 00:01:08.347
It doesn't mean that we don't

00:01:08.847 --> 00:01:08.914
--

00:01:08.914 --> 00:01:09.514
it doesn't mean that we agree

00:01:09.781 --> 00:01:10.015
on everything.

00:01:10.282 --> 00:01:11.483
We disagreed on many things.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.418
We've disagreed on Iran, we

00:01:13.685 --> 00:01:15.454
disagreed on other things, and

00:01:15.721 --> 00:01:16.855
we have agreed on many things.

00:01:16.855 --> 00:01:18.457
We've agreed that aligns has to

00:01:19.424 --> 00:01:20.292
be unshakable, because when you

00:01:20.859 --> 00:01:21.360
look at the Middle East, and

00:01:21.627 --> 00:01:22.294
you look at this part of the

00:01:22.861 --> 00:01:24.463
world, and you say, well, where

00:01:24.863 --> 00:01:28.300
do you have a bastion of common

00:01:28.867 --> 00:01:29.434
interests and common values?

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:30.469
It is Israel.

00:01:31.303 --> 00:01:31.837
Most Americans understand that.

00:01:34.273 --> 00:01:35.340
Our interests or sound, Israel

00:01:35.607 --> 00:01:38.877
remains diplomatic, it will be

00:01:38.911 --> 00:01:39.578
democratic after these

00:01:39.845 --> 00:01:41.313
democratic reforms, and be more

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:41.780
democratic.

00:01:42.414 --> 00:01:43.315
&gt;&gt; It's not democratic in the

00:01:43.582 --> 00:01:44.516
west bank though, that is the

00:01:44.883 --> 00:01:45.350
argument.

00:01:46.318 --> 00:01:47.319
&gt;&gt; I don't say that we don't

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:50.455
have right now military needs,

00:01:50.889 --> 00:01:52.324
but I'm saying that we can

00:01:52.891 --> 00:01:54.293
fashion them in a civilian

00:01:54.559 --> 00:01:55.727
agreement that maintains Israel

00:01:56.161 --> 00:01:56.495
overriding security.

00:01:56.895 --> 00:01:57.562
I don't think the Palestinians

00:01:57.829 --> 00:01:58.463
are there.

00:01:59.398 --> 00:02:00.399
What I will say is that our

00:02:00.899 --> 00:02:01.566
interests are converging.

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:05.370
As never before, because in the

00:02:05.637 --> 00:02:06.371
21st century, the future

00:02:06.905 --> 00:02:08.340
belongs to --

00:02:09.308 --> 00:02:10.442
Israel's the innovation nation.

00:02:11.343 --> 00:02:15.380
The other innovation nation, I

00:02:15.647 --> 00:02:16.515
think the U.S. Is the big one,

00:02:16.915 --> 00:02:17.349
U.S. --

00:02:17.349 --> 00:02:17.783
Israel is the second one.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:19.451
We provide valuable Intel,

00:02:19.718 --> 00:02:20.919
invaluable cybersecurity,

00:02:20.919 --> 00:02:22.354
weapons development, and

00:02:22.921 --> 00:02:23.422
civilian technology that is

00:02:23.689 --> 00:02:24.022
changing the world.

00:02:24.289 --> 00:02:25.590
That is why our Arab neighbors

00:02:25.857 --> 00:02:26.591
came to the Abraham accords.

00:02:27.292 --> 00:02:29.428
Both for security, but also for

00:02:29.695 --> 00:02:30.929
civilian technology which

00:02:30.929 --> 00:02:31.663
benders the lives of their

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:32.064
people.

00:02:32.364 --> 00:02:34.399
&gt;&gt; One thing I want to ask you

00:02:34.933 --> 00:02:36.468
about Russia and Ukraine is an

00:02:36.935 --> 00:02:38.437
adviser to zelenskyy flooded

00:02:38.704 --> 00:02:39.471
your name as somebody who might

00:02:39.738 --> 00:02:41.440
be a decent mediator between

00:02:41.707 --> 00:02:43.408
zelenskyy and Putin, between

00:02:44.109 --> 00:02:44.576
Putin and Russia.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:47.546
I am wondering if anybody in a

00:02:47.813 --> 00:02:48.613
position of power has ever

00:02:48.947 --> 00:02:50.148
floated that idea to you, and

00:02:50.415 --> 00:02:51.483
what would be your willingness

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.452
to take on that job?

00:02:54.286 --> 00:02:56.488
&gt;&gt; I was asked to do that early

00:02:56.955 --> 00:03:02.294
on in the breakout of the

00:03:02.561 --> 00:03:02.961
Ukraine war.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:06.631
I was an opposition leader at

00:03:06.965 --> 00:03:07.566
the time, and I said I have a

00:03:07.833 --> 00:03:07.933
rule.

00:03:08.333 --> 00:03:09.534
One prime minister at a time.

00:03:10.335 --> 00:03:11.403
One president at a time.

00:03:12.337 --> 00:03:13.739
&gt;&gt; Who asked you to do it?

00:03:14.272 --> 00:03:14.573
&gt;&gt; I was asked.

00:03:15.307 --> 00:03:16.608
I don't know if it was official,

00:03:16.975 --> 00:03:18.410
or if it was an official, and

00:03:18.977 --> 00:03:19.411
so I didn't even pursue it.

00:03:19.678 --> 00:03:20.645
I said there is a prime

00:03:20.979 --> 00:03:22.647
minister, let him decide what

00:03:22.981 --> 00:03:23.315
to do.

00:03:24.282 --> 00:03:25.450
He tried, did not succeed.

00:03:27.352 --> 00:03:29.354
If --

00:03:29.621 --> 00:03:30.455
&gt;&gt; We do you do it now?

00:03:30.989 --> 00:03:32.324
&gt;&gt; If I'm asked by both sides,

00:03:32.591 --> 00:03:34.359
and frankly if I'm asked by the

00:03:34.626 --> 00:03:35.427
United States, because I think

00:03:35.694 --> 00:03:37.329
that you cannot have too many

00:03:37.596 --> 00:03:41.299
cooks in the kitchen, and I am

00:03:41.566 --> 00:03:41.600
--

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.535
we have our own backyard to

00:03:43.802 --> 00:03:43.969
deal with.

00:03:44.336 --> 00:03:46.405
It is not that I don't think

00:03:46.671 --> 00:03:47.472
this is important, it's a

00:03:47.739 --> 00:03:48.640
monumental importance because

00:03:49.007 --> 00:03:49.708
of the piece of the world.

00:03:50.308 --> 00:03:53.345
As I think that the piece of

00:03:53.612 --> 00:03:54.579
the world's ex, stake getting

00:03:55.013 --> 00:03:56.314
nuclear weapons, it will be

00:03:56.581 --> 00:03:57.582
destabilizing the entire world.

00:03:58.316 --> 00:04:02.320
And so I think that really

00:04:02.587 --> 00:04:03.355
devoting my efforts to that,

00:04:03.622 --> 00:04:05.357
the piece ideas that I have,

00:04:05.624 --> 00:04:08.293
economic ideas, but if asked by

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:09.594
all relevant parties, I will

00:04:09.861 --> 00:04:10.395
certainly consider it.

00:04:11.296 --> 00:04:14.533
I'm not pushing myself, which

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:16.401
is --

00:04:16.668 --> 00:04:17.636
I have been around long enough

00:04:17.903 --> 00:04:21.273
to know that there needs to be

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:22.307
a ripe time.

00:04:22.574 --> 00:04:23.708
The ripe circumstances.

00:04:24.376 --> 00:04:26.411
If they arrive, I will

00:04:26.678 --> 00:04:27.045
certainly consider it.

00:04:27.312 --> 00:04:29.414
&gt;&gt; Trump has already launched a

00:04:29.681 --> 00:04:30.549
2024 presidential bid.

00:04:31.283 --> 00:04:33.585
You've said a few things about

00:04:33.852 --> 00:04:35.720
what he did for Israel while he

00:04:36.321 --> 00:04:36.555
was president.

00:04:36.822 --> 00:04:38.356
You've also criticized him for

00:04:39.257 --> 00:04:40.258
the insurrection that he

00:04:40.525 --> 00:04:41.393
incited, which you called quote,

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:42.527
a disgraceful act that must be

00:04:43.428 --> 00:04:43.795
vigorously condemned.

00:04:44.329 --> 00:04:45.630
And his recent, rather shocking

00:04:46.364 --> 00:04:47.566
willingness to sit down and

00:04:47.833 --> 00:04:49.334
break bread with holocaust

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.336
deniers and virulent

00:04:51.603 --> 00:04:51.803
antisemites.

00:04:52.471 --> 00:04:53.605
Nick Fuentes and Kanye west,

00:04:54.239 --> 00:04:54.439
for example.

00:04:54.706 --> 00:04:55.607
Do you have any concerns if he

00:04:55.874 --> 00:04:57.375
is back in the white house, do

00:04:57.642 --> 00:04:58.376
you think it's time for the

00:04:58.643 --> 00:04:59.611
Republican party to look for a

00:04:59.878 --> 00:05:01.613
new generation of leadership?

00:05:02.247 --> 00:05:04.316
&gt;&gt; First of all, I did praise

00:05:04.583 --> 00:05:05.350
president trump, because he did

00:05:05.617 --> 00:05:06.017
